<.page_title
  title="How it governs"
  subtitle="The delivery lifecycle, proof loop, and operating modes behind every governed change."
/>

<div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Governed delivery lifecycle</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Every change moves through the same loop, from stated intent to recorded evidence:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
      <li>
        Intent intake and execution briefs at
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">/new/session</code>
      </li>
      <li>Task graph, validation, and findings during execution</li>
      <li>Proof bundles, Ship Dashboard, and benchmarks as evidence</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Proof console loop</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Governance state lives outside the chat window, so evidence stays reviewable after the session ends:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
      <li>Session Control for active task state, risk, and approvals</li>
      <li>Findings turn policy violations into reviewable work</li>
      <li>Proof Browser for immutable evidence and rollback guidance</li>
      <li>Ship Dashboard and benchmarks for outcome evidence</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Autonomy and findings</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Severity maps to expected human gates; findings stay readable in plain language. LLM advisory is optional and needs a provider. See <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">docs/autonomy-and-findings.md</code>.
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
      <li>Low-risk guidance continues automatically with warnings when needed</li>
      <li>Medium-risk findings stay visible and route the operator toward a fix</li>
      <li>Destructive or high-risk actions are blocked or explicitly reviewed</li>
      <li>Governed repos keep the policy trail even when model features degrade</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Provider resolution and capabilities</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      ControlKeel resolves model access through the same fallback chain everywhere, so governance never depends on which source wins. Setup commands live in
      <.link navigate={~p"/docs/getting-started"} class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">getting started</.link>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">Resolution order</p>
    <ol class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-decimal ml-5">
      <li>Attached agent bridge when supported</li>
      <li>Workspace or service-account profile</li>
      <li>ControlKeel user default profile</li>
      <li>Project override</li>
      <li>Local Ollama</li>
      <li>Heuristic fallback</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="grid gap-4 pt-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="space-y-2 rounded-2xl border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Works without a provider</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
          <li>Governance and policy validation on agent actions</li>
          <li>Findings, proof bundles, and session audit trail</li>
          <li>MCP tools, skills, and agent attachments</li>
          <li>Benchmark runs and policy artifact management</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2 rounded-2xl border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Degrades without a provider</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
          <li>Execution brief compilation falls back to heuristics</li>
          <li>Advisory scanner only runs when a provider is available</li>
          <li>Model-backed guidance waits for a bridge, key, or Ollama model</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Operating modes</.section_title>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground list-disc ml-5">
      <li>Local mode ships with SQLite, Ollama, or heuristic fallback.</li>
      <li>
        Cloud mode connects orgs, projects, users, webhooks, and service accounts as shared governance evidence.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use benchmarks to collect bounded evidence before claiming a workflow is safer, cheaper, or faster.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Occupation-first onboarding</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Start from what best describes your work. ControlKeel picks the domain pack, interview language, and governance posture behind the scenes, so non-experts don't need to choose a framework first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Project rescue</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      If another tool already touched the repo, bootstrap it, run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel watch</code>, and use findings, proofs, and
      <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">ck_validate</code>
      to recover. Add governed proxy only when the tool points at compatible OpenAI or Anthropic endpoints.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
